Complexity of the Selection Sort Algorithm 
To sort a unsorted list with 'n' number of elements we need to make ((n-1)+(n-2)+(n-3)+......+1) = (n (n-1))/2 number 
of comparisions in the worst case. If the list already sorted, then it requires 'n' number of comparisions. 
Worst Case: O(n2) 
Best Case : O(n2) 
Average Case : O(n2) 
